Analyzing the theme of a literary passage and generating a thesis statement is a complex task that requires natural language processing and machine learning capabilities. While C# is a powerful programming language, it may not be the best choice for this task. However, we can use C# to extract specific information from the passage and perform some basic analysis.
Here's an example of how to use C# to extract information about George's characterization and generate a thesis statement:
```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;
class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        string passage = "George was a selfless and hardworking protagonist who always went unnoticed despite his efforts. He would wake up early every morning to tend to his farm, and he never complained about the long hours. Despite his hard work, he was never recognized for his contributions, and he often felt invisible.";
        // Extract information about George's characterization
        int selflessCount = Regex.Matches(passage, @"\bselfless\b").Count;
        int hardworkingCount = Regex.Matches(passage, @"\bhardworking\b").Count;
        int unnoticedCount = Regex.Matches(passage, @"\bunnoticed\b").Count;
