As an AI system using Latex, can you modify the following code in Java to find the sentence from a set of sentences that is most similar to $x$ using the Levenshtein distance metric? The sentences to use are: $\{s_1,s_2,s_3,s_4,s_5\}$ and $x$ is "I love to eat pizza". 
```java
public static int levenshteinDistance(String s1, String s2) {
    if (s1 == null || s2 == null) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Strings cannot be null");
    }
    int[][] distance = new int[s1.length() + 1][s2.length() + 1];
    for (int i = 0; i <= s1.length(); i++) {
        distance[i][0] = i;
    }
    for (int j = 1; j <= s2.length(); j++) {
        distance[0][j] = j;
    }
    for (int i = 1; i <= s1.length(); i++) {
        for (int j = 1; j <= s2.length(); j++) {
            int cost = s1.charAt(i - 1) == s2.charAt(j - 1) ? 0 : 1;
            distance[i][j] = Math.min(Math.min(distance[i - 1][j] + 1, distance[i][j - 1] + 1), distance[i - 1][j - 1] + cost);
        }
    }
    return distance[s1.length()][s2.length()];
}
public static String findMostSimilarSentence(String target, String[] sentences) {
    String mostSimilar = null;
    int lowestDistance = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
    for (String sentence : sentences) {
        int distance = levenshteinDistance(target, sentence);
        if (distance < lowestDistance) {
            lowestDistance = distance;
            mostSimilar = sentence;
        }
    }
    return mostSimilar;
}
```

