What is the formula for calculating correlation coefficient between customer loyalty and business profitability in PHP? Can you provide an example code using the formula to analyze a dataset and generate a summary report of the results? 
[formula]
$r=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^n (x_i-\bar{x})(y_i-\bar{y})}{\sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^n (x_i-\bar{x})^2}\sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^n (y_i-\bar{y})^2}}$
[PHP code]
<?php
//assuming the customer loyalty and business profitability data are stored in arrays $loyalty and $profitability respectively
//calculate mean of $loyalty and $profitability
$mean_loyalty=array_sum($loyalty)/count($loyalty);
$mean_profitability=array_sum($profitability)/count($profitability);
//calculate the numerator and denominator of the correlation coefficient formula
$numerator=0;
$denominator_loyalty=0;
$denominator_profitability=0;
for($i=0;$i<count($loyalty);$i++){
    $numerator+=($loyalty[$i]-$mean_loyalty)*($profitability[$i]-$mean_profitability);
    $denominator_loyalty+=pow(($loyalty[$i]-$mean_loyalty),2);
    $denominator_profitability+=pow(($profitability[$i]-$mean_profitability),2);
}
$denominator=sqrt($denominator_loyalty)*sqrt($denominator_profitability);
//calculate the correlation coefficient
$r=$numerator/$denominator;
//generate summary report based on the correlation coefficient value
if($r>0){
    echo "There is a positive correlation between customer loyalty and business profitability.";
}
elseif($r<0){
    echo "There is a negative correlation between customer loyalty and business profitability.";
}
else{
    echo "There is no correlation between customer loyalty and business profitability.";
}
?>

